1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,680
He stole the fucking Mona Lisa, then tried selling it by mail.

2
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:09,340
Paris, nineteen eleven. Vincenzo Peruggia used to work at the Louvre, so he knew the place.

3
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:13,560
And on a Monday when it was closed? He just walked out with it under his arm.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,200
No one noticed until the next damn day.

5
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:19,220
Double-tap if your job has worse security than that.

6
00:00:19,660 --> 00:00:24,200
The Louvre closed for a week. People lined up just to stare at the empty wall.

7
00:00:24,580 --> 00:00:27,180
And for over two years, the cops had nothing.

8
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:32,740
Two years. Zero leads. Total embarrassment for the most famous museum on Earth.

9
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:35,880
Because it was chilling in his tiny Paris apartment.

10
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:39,920
Then, in nineteen thirteen, he wrote to an art dealer in Florence.

11
00:00:40,520 --> 00:00:43,260
He offered the Mona Lisa for five hundred thousand lire.

12
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:46,040
Send this to whoever would still get caught bragging.

13
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:50,480
The dealer brought the Uffizi director to his hotel. And guess what they found?

14
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:54,040
They checked it. It was real. And then they called the cops.

15
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:57,940
Two years of hiding, ruined by one letter he wrote himself.

16
00:00:58,760 --> 00:01:00,380
Follow, 'cause the ending is wild.

17
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:03,160
His excuse? He said he did it for Italy.

18
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:07,420
A court gave him one year and fifteen days, and he served less than a year.

19
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:11,220
And the theft made the Mona Lisa the most famous painting in the world.

20
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:14,620
So was he an idiot or a patriot? One word.

